{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"botchy-felt-bluefish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`docs/llm-framework.md` §\"Comparing the engines\" says each engine record in `rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison` output names \"the verdict's `runner` and `model` and the provider-reported `ran_model`\". `_provenance` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py`) reads `ran_model` from `verdict[\"provider_provenance\"][\"ran_model\"]`. The plan-review verdict the harness gets back carries no `provider_provenance` key, so `ran_model` is always `null`.\n\nObserved 2026-11-13 on origin/main `aa1681bb531`. A live Bedrock run (`REBAR_LLM_CONFIG_FILE=.github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`, a 1-row labels file holding `0128-9a17-79db-450e`) completed both engines: pipeline `model=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, agentic `model=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, both `runner=pydantic_ai`, and both `ran_model: null`. A `rebar review-plan --output=json` verdict likewise has keys `advisory, blocking, coaching, coverage, …, model, runner, …` and no `provider_provenance`. The runner builds `provider_provenance` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, `ran_model` set after the call), and `plan_review/orchestrator.py` copies it into its output only when `provider_provenance` is passed in.\n\n## Approach\nTrace where the plan-review gate drops `provider_provenance` between the runner result and the verdict returned to the caller (`plan_review/workflow_ops.py` passes `ctx.inputs.get(\"provider_provenance\")`; `plan_review/agentic.py` reads `inputs.get(\"provider_provenance\")`), and carry the record of the call that produced the verdict onto the returned verdict for both engines. If several calls ran, use the one the verdict already names as its `model`. The harness then reads it unchanged. No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A plan-review verdict produced by either engine through a runner carries `provider_provenance.ran_model` naming the model that served the call; proved by a unit test with the fake runner for each engine.\n- [ ] `engine_comparison` records a non-null `ran_model` for each engine that ran; proved by `pytest tests/unit -k engine_comparison`.\n- [ ] Signed attestation material is unchanged (the field is verdict metadata, not signed material).\n\n## Testing\nAdd RED tests: one per engine asserting `provider_provenance.ran_model` on the returned verdict, and one harness test asserting a non-null `ran_model`. Run them, `make verify`, and a 1-row live comparison as above.","id":"8a82-3588-a6c6-4841","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Engine comparison records ran_model as null for both engines"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794590448254959663,"uuid":"e72d609f-cbb4-4ffd-b021-c49e9d077013"}